<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<xs:schema xmlns:xs="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">

<!--
Alabama Appellate Courts - Event Hearings API Response
=======================================================

This XSD documents the JSON API response structure from the Alabama
appellate courts event hearings endpoint.

API Endpoint:
https://publicportal-api.alappeals.gov/courts/{court-guid}/cms/events/{event-uuid}/hearings

URL Parameters:
- court-guid: Court GUID (e.g., "68f021c4-6a44-4735-9a76-5360b2e8af13")
- event-uuid: Event UUID from the events API

Query Parameters:
- page: Page number (0-indexed)
- size: Results per page (default: 100)
- sort: Sort field and direction (e.g., "orderBy,asc")

Response Format: JSON

The response contains all cases (hearings) scheduled for a specific oral
argument event/session.

Example Response Structure:
{
    "_embedded": {
        "results": [
            {
                "startDate": "2026-02-04T16:00:00.000+00:00",
                "hearingType": "Oral Argument",
                "hearingStatus": "Scheduled",
                "orderBy": 1,
                "event": {
                    "panelFlag": true
                },
                "caseHeader": {
                    "caseInstanceUUID": "1f4e6740-1e85-4099-b9c5-a187b5e46cea",
                    "caseNumber": "SC-2024-0672",
                    "caseTitle": "Ex parte Altonio Spencer (In re: Altonio Spencer v. State of Alabama)",
                    "courtID": "1"
                }
            },
            {
                "startDate": "2026-02-04T17:00:00.000+00:00",
                "hearingType": "Oral Argument",
                "hearingStatus": "Scheduled",
                "orderBy": 2,
                "event": {
                    "panelFlag": true
                },
                "caseHeader": {
                    "caseInstanceUUID": "652f4897-6d5d-4ecf-9a8f-b420dd548bac",
                    "caseNumber": "SC-2025-0370",
                    "caseTitle": "The New York Times Company v. Kai Spears.",
                    "courtID": "1"
                }
            }
        ]
    },
    "page": {
        "size": 100,
        "totalElements": 2,
        "totalPages": 1,
        "number": 0
    }
}

Hearing Fields:
- startDate: Specific hearing date/time (ISO 8601, more precise than event date)
- hearingType: Type of hearing (usually "Oral Argument")
- hearingStatus: Status (e.g., "Scheduled", "Completed", "Cancelled")
- orderBy: Order of hearing in the session (for sorting)

Case Header Fields:
- caseInstanceUUID: Unique identifier for the case (required)
- caseNumber: Official case number (e.g., "SC-2024-0672")
- caseTitle: Case name/title
- courtID: Numeric court identifier

Data Extraction:
- case_number: From caseHeader.caseNumber
- case_name: From caseHeader.caseTitle
- date_argued: Parsed from startDate (prefer this over event startDate if available)
- case_instance_uuid: From caseHeader.caseInstanceUUID
- court_id: Inherited from accumulated_data (already mapped from event)

Source URL Pattern:
https://publicportal.alappeals.gov/portal/court/{court-guid}/case/{case-uuid}

Output:
For each hearing, yield an AlaOralArgument object with:
- case_number
- court_id
- date_argued
- case_name
- source_url
- calendar_uuid (event UUID)
- case_instance_uuid

Notes:
- YouTube URLs are not provided in the API response
- They may need to be discovered separately or added manually
- The location is inherited from the parent event
-->

<xs:annotation>
    <xs:documentation>
        This is a documentation-only XSD for the Alabama Event Hearings API.
        The actual response is JSON, not XML.
    </xs:documentation>
</xs:annotation>

</xs:schema>
